{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-48142","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-55386","text":"OpenSentience Documentation"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-48144","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55387","marks":["bold"],"text":"\"Intelligence is not generation. It is structured accumulation.\""}]}],"id":"blk-48143","kind":"quote"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-48146","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55388","marks":["bold"],"text":"Part of the [&] Protocol stack"},{"id":"spn-55389","text":" · "},{"id":"spn-55390","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/ECOSYSTEM.md"}],"text":"Ecosystem overview"},{"id":"spn-55391","text":" · "},{"id":"spn-55392","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/PULSE/docs/THREE_PROTOCOL_STACK.md"}],"text":"Three-protocol stack"},{"id":"spn-55393","text":" · "},{"id":"spn-55394","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/STACK_COMPLETION.md"}],"text":"Stack status"}]}],"id":"blk-48145","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-48147","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55395","text":"Welcome to the documentation hub for "},{"id":"spn-55396","marks":["bold"],"text":"OpenSentience"},{"id":"spn-55397","text":" — the research arm and runtime governance layer of the [&] Protocol ecosystem."}]},{"id":"blk-48148","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55398","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-48149","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-55399","text":"What Is OpenSentience?"}]},{"id":"blk-48150","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55400","text":"OpenSentience is "},{"id":"spn-55401","marks":["bold"],"text":"not a product"},{"id":"spn-55402","text":". It is three things:"}]},{"id":"blk-48151","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55403","text":"1. "},{"id":"spn-55404","marks":["bold"],"text":"A research organization"},{"id":"spn-55405","text":" that publishes cognitive protocols — formal specifications grounding AI agent architecture in cognitive science. 2. "},{"id":"spn-55406","marks":["bold"],"text":"A thin governance shim"},{"id":"spn-55407","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-55408","marks":["code"],"text":"open_sentience"},{"id":"spn-55409","text":" hex package) that enforces permission, lifecycle, and autonomy policies on OTP-supervised agents. 3. "},{"id":"spn-55410","marks":["bold"],"text":"The home of two cross-cutting protocols"},{"id":"spn-55411","text":" — OS-009 PRISM (diagnostic benchmark) and OS-010 PULSE (loop manifest standard) — that sit above the eight cognitive primitives and turn the [&] portfolio into a measurable, composable, accountable agent substrate."}]},{"id":"blk-48152","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55412","text":"The research output is "},{"id":"spn-55413","marks":["bold"],"text":"ten numbered protocols"},{"id":"spn-55414","text":" organized in two layers:"}]},{"id":"blk-48153","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-48155","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55415","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive primitives"},{"id":"spn-55416","text":" (OS-001 through OS-008) — one capability each"}]}],"id":"blk-48154","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-48157","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55417","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cross-cutting protocols"},{"id":"spn-55418","text":" (OS-009 PRISM, OS-010 PULSE) — diagnostic + temporal layers above the primitives"}]}],"id":"blk-48156","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-48158","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55419","text":"The runtime output includes the Elixir governance package implementing OS-006 (shim) and OS-008 (harness), the "},{"id":"spn-55420","marks":["bold"],"text":"PRISM benchmark engine"},{"id":"spn-55421","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-55422","marks":["code"],"text":"/PRISM/"},{"id":"spn-55423","text":", Elixir/OTP, Fly.io, 6 MCP machines), and the "},{"id":"spn-55424","marks":["bold"],"text":"PULSE manifest standard"},{"id":"spn-55425","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-55426","marks":["code"],"text":"/PULSE/"},{"id":"spn-55427","text":", JSON Schema + reference manifests)."}]},{"id":"blk-48159","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55428","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-48160","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-55429","text":"The Ten Protocols"}]},{"id":"blk-48161","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-55430","text":"Cognitive Primitives (OS-001 — OS-008)"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-48163","spans":[{"id":"spn-55431","text":"Protocol"}]},{"id":"blk-48164","spans":[{"id":"spn-55432","text":"Name"}]},{"id":"blk-48165","spans":[{"id":"spn-55433","text":"Cognitive Basis"}]},{"id":"blk-48166","spans":[{"id":"spn-55434","text":"Implemented By"}]}],"id":"blk-48162","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-48167","spans":[{"id":"spn-55435","text":"OS-001"}]},{"id":"blk-48168","spans":[{"id":"spn-55436","text":"Continual Learning"}]},{"id":"blk-48169","spans":[{"id":"spn-55437","text":"Hippocampal consolidation"}]},{"id":"blk-48170","spans":[{"id":"spn-55438","text":"Graphonomous"}]}],[{"id":"blk-48171","spans":[{"id":"spn-55439","text":"OS-002"}]},{"id":"blk-48172","spans":[{"id":"spn-55440","text":"Topological Routing (κ)"}]},{"id":"blk-48173","spans":[{"id":"spn-55441","text":"Prefrontal gating"}]},{"id":"blk-48174","spans":[{"id":"spn-55442","text":"Graphonomous routing layer"}]}],[{"id":"blk-48175","spans":[{"id":"spn-55443","text":"OS-003"}]},{"id":"blk-48176","spans":[{"id":"spn-55444","text":"Deliberation Orchestrator"}]},{"id":"blk-48177","spans":[{"id":"spn-55445","text":"Dual-process theory"}]},{"id":"blk-48178","spans":[{"id":"spn-55446","text":"AgenTroMatic"}]}],[{"id":"blk-48179","spans":[{"id":"spn-55447","text":"OS-004"}]},{"id":"blk-48180","spans":[{"id":"spn-55448","text":"Attention Engine"}]},{"id":"blk-48181","spans":[{"id":"spn-55449","text":"Endogenous attention"}]},{"id":"blk-48182","spans":[{"id":"spn-55450","text":"Graphonomous attention module"}]}],[{"id":"blk-48183","spans":[{"id":"spn-55451","text":"OS-005"}]},{"id":"blk-48184","spans":[{"id":"spn-55452","text":"Model Tier Adaptation"}]},{"id":"blk-48185","spans":[{"id":"spn-55453","text":"Resource rationality"}]},{"id":"blk-48186","spans":[{"id":"spn-55454","text":"Graphonomous / Agentelic"}]}],[{"id":"blk-48187","spans":[{"id":"spn-55455","text":"OS-006"}]},{"id":"blk-48188","spans":[{"id":"spn-55456","text":"Agent Governance Shim"}]},{"id":"blk-48189","spans":[{"id":"spn-55457","text":"Executive function"}]},{"id":"blk-48190","spans":[{"id":"spn-55458","marks":["code"],"text":"open_sentience"},{"id":"spn-55459","text":" hex package"}]}],[{"id":"blk-48191","spans":[{"id":"spn-55460","text":"OS-007"}]},{"id":"blk-48192","spans":[{"id":"spn-55461","text":"Adversarial Robustness"}]},{"id":"blk-48193","spans":[{"id":"spn-55462","text":"Immune system"}]},{"id":"blk-48194","spans":[{"id":"spn-55463","text":"OpenSentience security module"}]}],[{"id":"blk-48195","spans":[{"id":"spn-55464","text":"OS-008"}]},{"id":"blk-48196","spans":[{"id":"spn-55465","text":"Agent Harness"}]},{"id":"blk-48197","spans":[{"id":"spn-55466","text":"Supervisory attentional system"}]},{"id":"blk-48198","spans":[{"id":"spn-55467","text":"OpenSentience harness module"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-48199","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-55468","text":"Cross-Cutting Protocols (OS-009, OS-010)"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-48201","spans":[{"id":"spn-55469","text":"Protocol"}]},{"id":"blk-48202","spans":[{"id":"spn-55470","text":"Name"}]},{"id":"blk-48203","spans":[{"id":"spn-55471","text":"Layer"}]},{"id":"blk-48204","spans":[{"id":"spn-55472","text":"Implemented By"}]}],"id":"blk-48200","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-48205","spans":[{"id":"spn-55473","marks":["bold"],"text":"OS-009"}]},{"id":"blk-48206","spans":[{"id":"spn-55474","marks":["bold"],"text":"PRISM"},{"id":"spn-55475","text":" — Protocol for Rating Iterative System Memory"}]},{"id":"blk-48207","spans":[{"id":"spn-55476","marks":["bold"],"text":"Diagnostic algebra"},{"id":"spn-55477","text":" (measures loops over time)"}]},{"id":"blk-48208","spans":[{"id":"spn-55478","marks":["code"],"text":"/PRISM/"},{"id":"spn-55479","text":" Elixir/OTP, Fly.io, 6 MCP machines, "},{"id":"spn-55480","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"https://prism.opensentience.org"}],"text":"prism.opensentience.org"}]}],[{"id":"blk-48209","spans":[{"id":"spn-55481","marks":["bold"],"text":"OS-010"}]},{"id":"blk-48210","spans":[{"id":"spn-55482","marks":["bold"],"text":"PULSE"},{"id":"spn-55483","text":" — Protocol for Uniform Loop State Exchange"}]},{"id":"blk-48211","spans":[{"id":"spn-55484","marks":["bold"],"text":"Temporal algebra"},{"id":"spn-55485","text":" (declares how loops cycle)"}]},{"id":"blk-48212","spans":[{"id":"spn-55486","marks":["code"],"text":"/PULSE/"},{"id":"spn-55487","text":" manifest standard, JSON Schema, reference manifests, "},{"id":"spn-55488","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"https://pulse.opensentience.org"}],"text":"pulse.opensentience.org"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-48213","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55489","text":"Each cognitive primitive maps a well-established cognitive science finding to a concrete software architecture. The cross-cutting protocols sit above them: PRISM measures how well a closed memory loop performs over time; PULSE declares how any loop in the [&] ecosystem cycles, nests, and signals across boundaries. Both are independent of one another and independent of [&] — a system may adopt one without the others."}]},{"id":"blk-48214","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55490","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-48215","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-55491","text":"Documentation Map"}]},{"id":"blk-48216","kind":"code","language":"text","text":":maxdepth: 1\n:caption: Homepages\n\n[&] Ampersand Box <https://ampersandboxdesign.com>\nGraphonomous <https://graphonomous.com>\nBendScript <https://bendscript.com>\nWebHost.Systems <https://webhost.systems>\nAgentelic <https://agentelic.com>\nAgenTroMatic <https://agentromatic.com>\nDelegatic <https://delegatic.com>\nDeliberatic <https://deliberatic.com>\nFleetPrompt <https://fleetprompt.com>\nGeoFleetic <https://geofleetic.com>\nOpenSentience <https://opensentience.org>\nSpecPrompt <https://specprompt.com>\nTickTickClock <https://ticktickclock.com>"},{"id":"blk-48217","kind":"code","language":"text","text":":maxdepth: 1\n:caption: Root Docs\n\n[&] Protocol Docs <https://docs.ampersandboxdesign.com>\nGraphonomous Docs <https://docs.graphonomous.com>\nBendScript Docs <https://docs.bendscript.com>\nWebHost.Systems Docs <https://docs.webhost.systems>\nAgentelic Docs <https://docs.agentelic.com>\nAgenTroMatic Docs <https://docs.agentromatic.com>\nDelegatic Docs <https://docs.delegatic.com>\nDeliberatic Docs <https://docs.deliberatic.com>\nFleetPrompt Docs <https://docs.fleetprompt.com>\nGeoFleetic Docs <https://docs.geofleetic.com>\nOpenSentience Docs <https://docs.opensentience.org>\nSpecPrompt Docs <https://docs.specprompt.com>\nTickTickClock Docs <https://docs.ticktickclock.com>"},{"id":"blk-48218","kind":"code","language":"text","text":":maxdepth: 2\n:caption: OpenSentience Docs\n\narchitecture\nquickstart\npositioning\necosystem-overview\ncompetitive-landscape\nharness-engineering\nruntime-walkthrough\ncomparison-table\nresearch\nfaq\nspec/README\nspec/OS-008-HARNESS\nspec/OS-009-PRISM-SPECIFICATION\nspec/OS-010-PULSE-SPECIFICATION\nspec/OS-E001-EMPIRICAL-EVALUATION"},{"id":"blk-48219","kind":"code","language":"text","text":":maxdepth: 1\n:caption: Skills\n\nskills/SKILLS\nskills/01_PROTOCOLS_OVERVIEW\nskills/02_AGENT_LIFECYCLE\nskills/03_PERMISSIONS\nskills/04_AUTONOMY_LEVELS\nskills/05_AUDIT_TRAILS\nskills/06_INTEGRATION\nskills/07_COGNITIVE_SCIENCE\nskills/08_ANTI_PATTERNS"},{"id":"blk-48220","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55492","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-48221","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-55493","text":"Suggested Reading Order"}]},{"id":"blk-48222","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55494","text":"If you are new to OpenSentience, follow this path:"}]},{"id":"blk-48223","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55495","text":"1. "},{"id":"spn-55496","marks":["bold"],"text":"This page"},{"id":"spn-55497","text":" — understand scope and structure 2. "},{"id":"spn-55498","marks":["bold"],"text":"positioning"},{"id":"spn-55499","text":" — where OpenSentience fits in the agent governance landscape 3. "},{"id":"spn-55500","marks":["bold"],"text":"architecture"},{"id":"spn-55501","text":" — how the governance shim is built (OTP internals) 4. "},{"id":"spn-55502","marks":["bold"],"text":"quickstart"},{"id":"spn-55503","text":" — install the hex package and run your first governed agent 5. "},{"id":"spn-55504","marks":["bold"],"text":"ecosystem-overview"},{"id":"spn-55505","text":" — how all ten protocols connect across the [&] ecosystem 6. "},{"id":"spn-55506","marks":["bold"],"text":"harness-engineering"},{"id":"spn-55507","text":" — the emerging discipline of harness design and OS-008's position 7. "},{"id":"spn-55508","marks":["bold"],"text":"runtime-walkthrough"},{"id":"spn-55509","text":" — follow a concrete agent through governance + harness orchestration 8. "},{"id":"spn-55510","marks":["bold"],"text":"competitive-landscape"},{"id":"spn-55511","text":" — how OpenSentience compares to alternative approaches 9. "},{"id":"spn-55512","marks":["bold"],"text":"comparison-table"},{"id":"spn-55513","text":" — quick-reference feature comparison 10. "},{"id":"spn-55514","marks":["bold"],"text":"research"},{"id":"spn-55515","text":" — cognitive science grounding for each protocol 11. "},{"id":"spn-55516","marks":["bold"],"text":"faq"},{"id":"spn-55517","text":" — fill in remaining questions 12. "},{"id":"spn-55518","marks":["bold"],"text":"skills/"},{"id":"spn-55519","text":" — hands-on implementation skills for the governance shim"}]},{"id":"blk-48224","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55520","text":"For deep protocol specifics:"}]},{"id":"blk-48225","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-48227","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55521","marks":["bold"],"text":"spec/README"},{"id":"spn-55522","text":" — the full technical specification (all ten protocols)"}]}],"id":"blk-48226","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-48229","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55523","marks":["bold"],"text":"spec/OS-008-HARNESS"},{"id":"spn-55524","text":" — the Agent Harness Protocol specification"}]}],"id":"blk-48228","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-48231","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55525","marks":["bold"],"text":"spec/OS-009-PRISM-SPECIFICATION"},{"id":"spn-55526","text":" — PRISM diagnostic benchmark protocol"}]}],"id":"blk-48230","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-48233","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55527","marks":["bold"],"text":"spec/OS-010-PULSE-SPECIFICATION"},{"id":"spn-55528","text":" — PULSE loop manifest standard"}]}],"id":"blk-48232","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-48235","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55529","marks":["bold"],"text":"spec/OS-E001-EMPIRICAL-EVALUATION"},{"id":"spn-55530","text":" — empirical evaluation of topology-aware continual learning"}]}],"id":"blk-48234","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-48236","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55531","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-48237","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-55532","text":"Documentation index"}]},{"id":"blk-48238","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55533","text":"Linked index of every page in this set (renders on GitHub and in the docs atlas; the toctrees above drive the Sphinx build):"}]},{"id":"blk-48239","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55534","marks":["bold"],"text":"Guides"}]},{"id":"blk-48240","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-48242","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55535","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/quickstart.md"}],"text":"Quickstart"}]}],"id":"blk-48241","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-48244","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55536","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/runtime-walkthrough.md"}],"text":"Runtime Walkthrough"}]}],"id":"blk-48243","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-48246","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55537","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/positioning.md"}],"text":"Positioning — The Missing Constraint: Runtime Governance in the Agent Stack"}]}],"id":"blk-48245","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-48248","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55538","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/competitive-landscape.md"}],"text":"Competitive Landscape — Agent Governance and Runtime Enforcement"}]}],"id":"blk-48247","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-48250","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55539","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/comparison-table.md"}],"text":"Comparison — OpenSentience vs. Alternatives"}]}],"id":"blk-48249","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-48252","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55540","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/ecosystem-overview.md"}],"text":"Ecosystem Overview — How the Protocols Connect"}]}],"id":"blk-48251","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-48254","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55541","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/research.md"}],"text":"Research Overview"}]}],"id":"blk-48253","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-48256","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55542","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/faq.md"}],"text":"FAQ"}]}],"id":"blk-48255","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-48258","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55543","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/skills/SKILLS.md"}],"text":"Agent Skills"}]}],"id":"blk-48257","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-48259","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55544","marks":["bold"],"text":"Specifications"}]},{"id":"blk-48260","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-48262","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55545","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/spec/OS-011-EMBODIMENT.md"}],"text":"OS-011 — Embodiment Protocol"}]}],"id":"blk-48261","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-48264","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55546","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/spec/OS-E001-EMPIRICAL-EVALUATION.md"}],"text":"OS-E001 — Empirical Evaluation of Topology-Aware Continual Learning"}]}],"id":"blk-48263","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-48265","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55547","marks":["bold"],"text":"UX & build prompts"}]},{"id":"blk-48266","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-48268","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55548","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/ux/user-stories-embodiment.md"}],"text":"Embodiment (body-browser + body-os) — User Stories"}]}],"id":"blk-48267","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-48270","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55549","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/prompts/OS-008-BUILD.md"}],"text":"OS-008 Agent Harness Protocol — Implementation Build Prompt"}]}],"id":"blk-48269","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-48271","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-55550","text":"The Three Enforcement Layers"}]},{"id":"blk-48272","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55551","text":"OpenSentience provides three layers of runtime enforcement:"}]},{"id":"blk-48273","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"OS-008 Harness:   \"Has this agent followed the correct process?\"\n                   Pipeline ordering, quality gates, sprint contracts\n\nOS-006 Shim:      \"Is this agent allowed to do this?\"\n                   Permissions, lifecycle, autonomy levels\n\nOS-007 Security:  \"Is this agent under attack?\"\n                   Threat detection, identity verification, circuit breakers"},{"id":"blk-48274","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55552","text":"All three log to the same append-only audit trail, creating a unified compliance record from protocol to permission to pipeline."}]},{"id":"blk-48275","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55553","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-48276","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-55554","text":"The Three-Protocol Stack"}]},{"id":"blk-48277","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55555","text":"Above the cognitive primitives, OpenSentience publishes three sibling protocols that together turn the [&] portfolio into a measurable, composable, accountable agent substrate:"}]},{"id":"blk-48278","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  PRISM (OS-009) — measures loops over time   diagnostic │\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  PULSE (OS-010) — declares loops + signals    temporal  │\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  [&] Protocol     — composes capabilities     structural│\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘"},{"head":[{"id":"blk-48280","spans":[{"id":"spn-55556","text":"Layer"}]},{"id":"blk-48281","spans":[{"id":"spn-55557","text":"Question"}]},{"id":"blk-48282","spans":[{"id":"spn-55558","text":"Artifact"}]}],"id":"blk-48279","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-48283","spans":[{"id":"spn-55559","text":"[&]"}]},{"id":"blk-48284","spans":[{"id":"spn-55560","text":"What can each agent do, and how do they compose?"}]},{"id":"blk-48285","spans":[{"id":"spn-55561","marks":["code"],"text":"*.ampersand.json"}]}],[{"id":"blk-48286","spans":[{"id":"spn-55562","text":"PULSE"}]},{"id":"blk-48287","spans":[{"id":"spn-55563","text":"How do their processes cycle and signal each other?"}]},{"id":"blk-48288","spans":[{"id":"spn-55564","marks":["code"],"text":"*.pulse.json"},{"id":"spn-55565","text":" (loop manifest)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-48289","spans":[{"id":"spn-55566","text":"PRISM"}]},{"id":"blk-48290","spans":[{"id":"spn-55567","text":"How well do those cycles actually work over time?"}]},{"id":"blk-48291","spans":[{"id":"spn-55568","text":"Diagnostic reports + leaderboards"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-48292","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55569","text":"A loop is "},{"id":"spn-55570","marks":["bold"],"text":"PULSE-conforming"},{"id":"spn-55571","text":" if its manifest validates against "},{"id":"spn-55572","marks":["code"],"text":"pulse-loop-manifest.v0.1.json"},{"id":"spn-55573","text":" and its runtime passes the 12-test conformance suite. A system is "},{"id":"spn-55574","marks":["bold"],"text":"PRISM-evaluable"},{"id":"spn-55575","text":" automatically once it is PULSE-conforming — PRISM's "},{"id":"spn-55576","marks":["code"],"text":"compose"},{"id":"spn-55577","text":" phase reads the manifest, injects scenarios at the declared "},{"id":"spn-55578","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve"},{"id":"spn-55579","text":" boundary, and observes outcomes via the declared "},{"id":"spn-55580","marks":["code"],"text":"learn"},{"id":"spn-55581","text":" phase. Adoption order is typically [&] → PULSE → PRISM."}]},{"id":"blk-48293","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55582","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-48294","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-55583","text":"Relationship to the [&] Ecosystem"}]},{"id":"blk-48295","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55584","text":"OpenSentience occupies the "},{"id":"spn-55585","marks":["bold"],"text":"governance and research layer"},{"id":"spn-55586","text":" of the [&] stack:"}]},{"id":"blk-48296","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"  [&] Protocol        — capability composition (what an agent CAN do)\n  OpenSentience       — governance + harness (what an agent MAY do, and how)\n  Graphonomous        — memory + learning (OS-001, OS-002, OS-004, OS-005)\n  AgenTroMatic        — deliberation (OS-003)\n  Delegatic           — policy authoring (feeds into OS-006 enforcement)\n  Agentelic           — agent manifests (consumed by OS-006 install)\n  FleetPrompt         — marketplace (agents enter governance on install)\n  SpecPrompt          — acceptance criteria (consumed by OS-008 quality gates)"},{"id":"blk-48297","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55587","text":"The governance shim wraps any OTP "},{"id":"spn-55588","marks":["code"],"text":"child_spec"},{"id":"spn-55589","text":". It does not replace the supervised process — it interposes permission checks, lifecycle management, autonomy control, pipeline enforcement, and audit logging around it."}]},{"id":"blk-48298","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55590","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-48299","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-55591","text":"Founding Thesis"}]},{"id":"blk-48300","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55592","text":"OpenSentience exists because intelligence without governance is generation without accumulation. The ten protocols formalize what structured accumulation requires: memory that consolidates, routing that detects cycles, deliberation that resolves conflict, attention that prioritizes, resources that adapt, governance that enforces boundaries, security that detects threats, a harness that orchestrates the entire pipeline, "},{"id":"spn-55593","marks":["bold"],"text":"diagnostics that measure whether the loop actually learns"},{"id":"spn-55594","text":" (PRISM), and a "},{"id":"spn-55595","marks":["bold"],"text":"temporal manifest"},{"id":"spn-55596","text":" that lets every loop in the ecosystem declare how it cycles and signals (PULSE)."}]},{"id":"blk-48301","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55597","text":"The shim is deliberately thin. Governance should cost less than 1% of the system it governs. PULSE is a manifest standard with no required runtime. PRISM runs as a separate benchmark engine that any system can opt into via its PULSE manifest."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaierap4ia4zglj53iy6ldpd54h7gsdmz3z3ugahkk7327ad5xvhux3boa","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}